# Copy to `.env` and edit. `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# Everything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is bundled into the shipped app and is therefore NOT SECRET.
# It can be read straight out of the APK. Only ever put a value here whose worst case is an
# exhausted quota — never a key attached to a payment method or to anything that can be spent.

# Which Solana cluster the app talks to. Anything other than `devnet` means mainnet.
EXPO_PUBLIC_CLUSTER=

# The RPC provider the app reads balances from.
#
# Leave empty and the app runs on https://api.mainnet-beta.solana.com, which is heavily rate
# limited and explicitly not intended for production traffic — fine for development, not for a
# release build.
#
# For a release, use a free-tier provider key. Helius: sign up at https://helius.dev, then
# Dashboard → API Keys, and paste the full URL here, for example
#   https://mainnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
#
# If this endpoint fails or runs out of quota the app falls back to the public one on its own,
# so a burned key degrades the app rather than breaking it. See docs/06-SOLANA.md.
EXPO_PUBLIC_RPC_URL=
